Substantially all of the EVM behaviour this package exposes -- the interpreter,
the precompiles, the fee market, gas accounting, EIP-161 state clearing,
EIP-6780, EIP-2930 access-list warming, EIP-4844 and EIP-7702 handling -- is
revm's work, driven through revm's own code paths. This package contributes a
build configuration, a host database adapter, a binary outcome encoding and a
typed JavaScript API.


Other components compiled into the artifact
-------------------------------------------

The artifact statically links revm's pure-Rust cryptography backends, each under
its own permissive licence (MIT and/or Apache-2.0):

    k256, elliptic-curve, ecdsa            (ecrecover, EIP-7702 authority recovery)
    sha2, ripemd, blake2                   (hash precompiles)
    aurora-engine-modexp                   (modexp)
    ark-bn254, ark-bls12-381, ark-ec, ark-ff, ark-poly   (bn254, BLS12-381, KZG)
    p256                                   (secp256r1 / RIP-7212)
    alloy-primitives and the alloy EIP crates
    revm-* workspace crates

Run `cargo tree` in `crates/` for the complete, exact dependency set of a given
build, and `cargo about` or an equivalent tool if you need a full licence
manifest for compliance purposes.
